# Susanna - Amerikaans lied (Oh! Susanna) van Stephen Foster
# Geschreven door Stephen Foster (overleden 1864), in 1848 uitgegeven door W. C. Peters
# & Co. in Cincinnati (Wikipedia (en), "Oh! Susanna"). Publiek domein.
# Overgenomen uit SUSANNA (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). Tikfouten hersteld: "alle night", "saud",
# "comming", en hoofdletters voor Alabama en Louisiana. De bron noteert het refrein
# een keer; hier staat het na elk couplet.
{title: Susanna}
{meta: id susanna}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: Stephen Foster}
{composer: Stephen Foster}
{year: 1848}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit SUSANNA (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); schrijver en jaar via Wikipedia (en), Oh! Susanna}
{meta: tag kampvuur}
{meta: tag volkslied}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse}
I [D]come from [E7]Alaba[A7]ma with a banjo on my knee
I'm [D]going to Louisiana, [G]my [D]true love for [A7]to [D]see
it [D]rained all night the day I [E7]left the [A7]weather it was dry
the [D]sun so hot I [G]froze to [D]death Susanna [A7]don't you [D]cry[D7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Oh Susan[A7]na oh don't [D]you cry for [A7]me
I come [D]from Alabama
[G]with a [D]banjo [A7]on my [D]knee
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
I had a dream the other night when everything was still
I thought I saw Susanna a coming down the hill
A red red rose was in her cheek, a tear was in her eye
I said to her, Susanna girl, Susanna don't you cry
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
I soon will be in New Orleans and I will look around
and when I find Susanna I will fall upon the ground
but if I do not find her then I'm surely bound
to die and when I'm dead and buried Susanna don't you cry
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
